<title>CANADA: Canada body says US ups oat herbicide tolerance.</title>
<headline>Canada body says US ups oat herbicide tolerance.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Environmental Protection Agency raised its herbicide residue tolerance level on oat imports to 20 parts per million of glyphosate from 0.1 ppm, Canadian Grain Commission said.</p>
<p>Canada exported 1.2 million tonnes of oats in crop year 1996/97 (Aug/July), CGC statistics show.</p>
<p>Most Canadian oat exports go to Minneapolis-based millers for consumer cereals or are used in animal feed.</p>
<p>Glyphosate is a herbicide used to control weeds.</p>
<p>Canada's glyphosate residue tolerance level on oats is 10 ppm.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
